{{Quote|Retreat, you must. On the moon below is my mission. There, I must go.|Yoda, to [[Clone Captain]] [[Zak]]|audio=YodaMyMission.flac|<ref name="Ambush" />}}
The '''Battle of Rugosa''',<ref name="Blasters">{{EncyclopediaCite|Blasters and Ranged Weapons}}</ref> also known as the '''Ambush on Rugosa''',<ref name="HC 38">{{HelmetCollectionCite|38|Highlights of the Saga}}</ref> was a mission that took place during the [[Clone Wars]] on the [[moon]] [[Rugosa]]. The [[Galactic Republic]] aimed to create a base to combat the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. The mission proved successful as the spirited fighting of the [[Jedi]] impressed the [[Toydarian]] [[king]], [[Katuunko]], who agreed to ally with them.<ref name="Ambush" />

==Prelude==
{{Main|The Matter of Using Toydarian Territory to Aid the Shipment of Relief Supplies to the Citizens of Ryloth|Mission to Toydaria|Battle of Ryloth|Invasion of Ryloth}}
The mission to Rugosa was not Katuunko's [[The Matter of Using Toydarian Territory to Aid the Shipment of Relief Supplies to the Citizens of Ryloth|first dealing]] with the Republic, having helped them [[Mission to Toydaria|clandestinely smuggle]] relief supplies to the [[Invasion of Ryloth|beleaguered]] [[Twi'lek]]s of [[Ryloth]] during the [[Battle of Ryloth]].<ref name="Supply Lines">{{TCW|Supply Lines}}</ref> While the fighting would continue for some time still,<ref name="Timelines" /> the supplies helped to maintain a grouping of Twi'lek refugees under the rebel leader [[Cham Syndulla]],<ref name="Supply Lines" /> whose forces would be instrumental in the [[Battle of Lessu|eventual liberation of Ryloth]].<ref name="Timelines" />

==The battle==
Katuunko arrived on the neutral moon of Rugosa on his yacht, the ''[[Thief's Eye]]'', with two members of the [[Toydarian Guard]]. As they puzzled over the late appearance of the Jedi, they were surprised by the arrival of Separatist commander [[Asajj Ventress]], who had been sent on behalf of her master, [[Count]] [[Dooku]], to attempt to convince the king to instead side with the Separatists. To convince the king that the Jedi were too weak to protect his system, Dooku had two frigates ambush the Republic cruiser carrying the Republic envoy, [[Jedi Master]] [[Yoda]] and several clones of the [[Coruscant Guard]]. Yoda, however, made it to the moon's surface in an escape pod, so instead, the Separatists turned the meeting into a contest of strength. Ventress would send her best troops to capture the Jedi, with their success or failure deciding who Katuunko would join. Yoda accepted the challenge despite Katuunko's misgivings and the king insisted that Yoda be given a fair fight. Ventress agreed despite intending nothing of the sort and deployed a full battalion of droids and tanks to capture Yoda.<ref name="Ambush" />

Under the command of [[224]], the droid forces found the Republic delegation but the moon's large coral formations prevented their tanks from reaching them. Droid patrols advanced on foot, but were easily destroyed by the clones and Jedi, though the former were forced to retreat by a squad of [[B2-series super battle droid]]s, one of whom injured Lieutenant Thire before Yoda arrived and swiftly destroyed them. During this time, King Katuunko regularly communicated with Yoda until Ventress destroyed his communicator in anger, vowing that the Jedi would not escape her.<ref name="Ambush" />

Yoda then confronted the full force himself, dismantling droids and tanks single-handedly with only his lightsaber, including 224 himself. When Ventress attempted to contact 224 and was informed of his destruction, as well as Katuunko's stated faith in the Jedi, she broke the terms of the challenge by deploying droidekas into battle. Yoda's clones, who had been watching the Jedi cut his way through the droids with hearty amusement, spotted the inbound droidekas and devised a plan to take them out as Yoda finished destroying the last tank. Using their sole remaining rocket, the clones brought down an adjacent cliff face on the droidekas, destroying them and winning the challenge.<ref name="Ambush" />

Having his mind made, Katuunko contacted Dooku and stated his intention to join the Republic, citing his refusal to deal with those who broke their words as Ventress had done when she sent in the droidekas. After deciding that negotiations would be more fruitful with Katuunko's successor, Dooku spitefully ordered Ventress to murder the king. Katuunko's guards attempted to shoot her in defense of their monarch, but she easily deflected their shots before Force-pushing them away and moved to kill the king with her paired lightsabers. The red blades were halted inches from Katuunko's head by Yoda, however, and Ventress' droids were swiftly dealt with by the clones. Though Ventress proclaimed no fear of the Jedi, Yoda disarmed her with the Force before advising her to surrender. Instead, Ventress detonated pre-planted explosives which destroyed the king's yacht, escaping as Yoda was forced to protect himself and his allies from the falling debris. With Ventress gone, Katuunko stated that negotiations were unnecessary and presented Yoda with his ceremonial sword, signifying the beginning of Toydaria's membership in the Republic just as a Republic cruiser arrived in orbit to extract them.<ref name="Ambush" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Ambush on Rugosa first appeared in "[[Ambush]],"<ref name="Ambush" /> the first episode of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''' [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]], which originally aired on [[October 3]], [[2008]].<ref name="Ambush Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode001.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Ambush}}</ref> The ambush was later first identified the thirty-eighth issue of the [[Star Wars Helmet Collection]] magazine series published by [[De Agostini]] in [[2017]].<ref name="HC 38" />

